// Title: Azure OpenAI - New API Key Regeneration or Role Grant
// Description: Detects key regeneration/listing and new role assignments
//   (e.g. "Cognitive Services OpenAI User/Contributor") on Azure OpenAI
//   resources. A new principal gaining access to an AI resource, or a key
//   being regenerated outside a known rotation schedule, is a common
//   persistence or privilege-escalation step after initial compromise of
//   an Azure identity - it grants ongoing access to a resource that can
//   itself be abused for cost harvesting, data exposure via prompts sent
//   through it, or as a pivot point.
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1098 (Account Manipulation), T1078.004 (Valid Accounts:
//   Cloud Accounts)
// Data source: Azure Activity Log (AzureActivity table)
// False positives: Legitimate scheduled key rotations and normal
//   onboarding of new applications/service principals to an Azure OpenAI
//   resource. Cross-reference Caller against your change management
//   records; alert with higher confidence on grants/regenerations outside
//   business hours or by callers with no prior history against this
//   resource.

AzureActivity
| where TimeGenerated > ago(1d)
| where ResourceProviderValue == "MICROSOFT.COGNITIVESERVICES"
| where OperationNameValue has_any ("regenerateKey", "listKeys", "roleAssignments/write")
| where ActivityStatusValue == "Success"
| project TimeGenerated, Caller, CallerIpAddress, OperationNameValue, Resource, ResourceGroup, ActivityStatusValue
| order by TimeGenerated desc
